BND-17: keep the time of the daily maximum temperature after sunrise

climate::updateTempTimes() put both sunrise and the time of the maximum at
noon when the sun does not rise, so the temperature stepped from Tmin to Tmax
at once; for days shorter than 3 h it put the maximum before sunrise, as
legacy does, and Tmax was never reached. Treat polar night as legacy does (a
zero half-day length, with the longitude correction) and keep the hour of the
maximum at least 1 h after sunrise, as the legacy patch does. Days of 4 h or
longer are unchanged.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply BND-17_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/hydrology/Climate.cpp b/src/engine/hydrology/Climate.cpp
index 4c9c135..edaf009 100644
--- a/src/engine/hydrology/Climate.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/hydrology/Climate.cpp
@@ -194,9 +194,9 @@ void updateTempTimes(ClimateState& state, int doy) {
 
     double hrsr, hrss;
     if (arg >= 1.0) {
-        // Polar night — sun never rises; use noon for both
-        hrsr = 12.0;
-        hrss = 12.0;
+        // Polar night — sun never rises: zero half-day length (legacy)
+        hrsr = 12.0 + state.dtlong;
+        hrss = 12.0 + state.dtlong - 3.0;
     } else if (arg <= -1.0) {
         // Midnight sun — sun never sets
         hrsr = 0.0;
@@ -206,6 +206,9 @@ void updateTempTimes(ClimateState& state, int doy) {
         hrsr = 12.0 - hrang + state.dtlong;
         hrss = 12.0 + hrang + state.dtlong - 3.0; // max temp ~3 h before actual sunset
     }
+    // Days shorter than 4 h (polar winter): the max temp hour would come less
+    // than 1 h after, or even before, sunrise; keep it 1 h after sunrise.
+    if (hrss < hrsr + 1.0) hrss = hrsr + 1.0;
 
     state.hrsr  = hrsr;
     state.hrss  = hrss;
